    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(x\\ne1,2,\\) cross-multiplication gives \\[ x-2=2(x-1)=2x-2, \\] so \\(x=0.\\) This value makes both original denominators nonzero and satisfies the equality.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Cross-multiply, while remembering that \\(x\\ne1,2\\)",
        "Solve \\(x-2=2x-2\\)"
      ],
